cpsutil is a command line utility tool for CPS3 games.

different CPS3 emulators expect differently formatted roms, this tool can convert between the two.
a split rom looks like this:
	game-simm1.0, game-simm1.1, game-simm1.2, game-simm1.3
a combined rom looks like this:
	10, 20, 30, 31

usage:
	cpsutil < -g [gamename] > -i [inputs] ( -combine, -split, -encrypt, -decrypt ) -o [output]
input should be your rom, the output and input can be a zip file or a directory.
the tasks can be chained together

example usage:
	cpsutil -i game.zip -combine -o output.zip
this will take a split rom (game.zip), combine it, and dump it to output.zip.
the tool tries to detect what cps3 game you're using based on the name, you can manually input it as well.

example usage:
	cpsutil -g sfiii3 -i ./romdirectory -combine -o ./output

chaining example usage:
	cpsutil -i game.zip -combine -split -o output.zip
this will take a split rom, combine it, and then split it again. there is no reason to do this

chaining example usage:
	cpsutil -i ./game -encrypt -split -o output.zip
this will take a combined rom, encrypt and then split it. useful for rom hacks